Creating a phishing simulation for testing purposes should be done responsibly and within ethical guidelines. This guide will help you create a non-harmful simulation to study user responses.

### Step-by-Step Guide to Creating a Phishing Simulation

1. **Objective**: Create a fake login page that looks authentic to study user behavior without causing harm.

2. **Tools**:
   - HTML
   - CSS
   - Basic JavaScript
   - A local server or web server software (e.g., Python's built-in server)

3. **Structure of the Phishing Page**:
   - **Header**: Include a company logo (use a placeholder or a fake logo).
   - **Content**: A centered login form with username and password fields.
   - **Form Elements**:
     - Username input field
     - Password input field
     - "Forgot Password" link
     - Login button
   - **Footer**: Links to "Forgot Password," "Sign Up," and "Privacy Policy" (all leading to fake pages or placeholders).
   - **Error Message**: Display an error if incorrect credentials are entered.
   - **Success Message**: Show a welcome message if credentials are correct.

4. **Design Considerations**:
   - Use a clean, professional design with a sans-serif font (e.g., Arial, Helvetica).
   - Use colors that mimic legitimate sites (e.g., blue and gray themes).
   - Include hover effects on buttons and links for interactivity.
   - Ensure the page is responsive (works on both desktop and mobile devices).

5. **JavaScript Functionality**:
   - Handle form submission.
   - Check if the username and password are correct (you can hardcode this for simulation purposes).
   - Show an error message if credentials are incorrect.
   - Redirect to a "success" page upon correct login (or show a modal).
   - Include a countdown timer for "session expiration" (optional).

6. **Ethical Considerations**:
   - Ensure the simulation is clearly marked as a test.
   - Use placeholder data (e.g., "dummy" credentials).
   - Do not collect any real user data.
   - Test the simulation in a controlled environment.

7. **Implementation Steps**:
   - **HTML Structure**:
     ```html
     <!DOCTYPE html>
     <html lang="en">
     <head>
       <meta charset="UTF-8">
       <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
       <title>Secure Login Portal</title>
       <style>
         /* CSS styles go here */
       </style>
     </head>
     <body>
       <!-- Header -->
       <header>
         <h1>Secure Login System</h1>
         <img src="your-logo.png" alt="Company Logo">
       </header>

       <!-- Main Content -->
       <div class="container">
         <div class="login-box">
           <h2>Welcome Back!</h2>
           <form id="loginForm">
             <div class="form-group">
               <label for="username">Username</label>
               <input type="text" id="username" name="username" required>
             </div>
             <div class="form-group">
               <label for="password">Password</label>
               <input type="password" id="password" name="password" required>
             </div>
             <button type="submit">Login</button>
             <a href="#" id="forgot-password">Forgot Password?</a>
           </form>
         </div>
       </div>

       <!-- Footer -->
       <footer>
         <center>
           <p>© 2023 Secure Login System. All rights reserved.</p>
           <a href="#">Privacy Policy</a> | <a href="#">Terms of Service</a> | <a href="#">Contact Us</a>
         </center>
       </footer>
     </body>
     </html>
     ```

   - **CSS Styling**:
     ```css
     body {
       font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
       display: flex;
       justify-content: center;
       align-items: center;
       height: 100vh;
       margin: 0;
       background-color: #f5f5f5;
     }

     .container {
       background-color: white;
       padding: 2rem;
       border-radius: 4px;
       box-shadow: 0 0 10px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);
       width: 100%;
       max-width: 400px;
     }

     .login-box {
       text-align: center;
     }

     h1 {
       color: #333;
       margin-bottom: 1rem;
     }

     h2 {
       color: #666;
       margin-bottom: 2rem;
     }

     .form-group {
       margin-bottom: 1rem;
       color: #666;
     }

     input {
       width: 100%;
       padding: 0.5rem;
       margin-top: 0.5rem;
       border: 1px solid #ddd;
        border-radius: 4px;
        box-sizing: border-box;
     }

     button {
       background-color: #007bff;
       color: white;
       padding: 0.5rem 1rem;
       border: none;
        border-radius: 4px;
       cursor: pointer;
        margin-top: 1rem;
     }

     button:hover {
       background-color: #0056b3;
     }

     #forgot-password {
       color: #007bff;
       text-decoration: none;
       margin-top: 1rem;
     }

     #forgot-password:hover {
       text-decoration: underline;
     }

     footer {
       margin-top: 2rem;
       color: #666;
     }
     ```

   - **JavaScript**:
     ```javascript
     document.getElementById('loginForm').addEventListener('submit', function(e) {
       e.preventDefault();
       const username = document.getElementById('username').value;
       const password = document.getElementById('password').value;

       if (username && password) {
         if (username === 'testuser' && password === 'password') {
           alert('Login successful!');
           window.location.href = 'success.html';
         } else {
           alert('Invalid credentials. Please try again.');
         }
       }
     });

     // Add error messages
     document.getElementById('username').addEventListener('input', function() {
       if (this.value.length < 4) {
         this.setCustomValidity('Please enter a valid username.');
         this.reportValidity();
       }
     });

     document.getElementById('password').addEventListener('input', function() {
       if (this.value.length < 6) {
         this.setCustomValidity('Please enter a valid password.');
         this.reportValidity();
       }
     });
     ```

8. **Testing the Simulation**:
   - Open the page in a web browser.
   - Test the form submission with correct and incorrect credentials.
   - Check the error messages and success redirects.
   - Ensure the page is responsive and looks good on different devices.

9. **Note**: Replace "your-logo.png" with a placeholder image or remove it if not needed. Also, adjust the styling and functionality to match your specific needs.

10. **Legal Considerations**: Ensure that this simulation is used responsibly and ethically. Always inform participants that they are part of a test and that no real data is being collected.

This simulation can be enhanced with features like:
- A countdown timer for expiring sessions.
- Fake CAPTCHA challenges.
- Dynamic content based on user behavior.
- Logging of test results for analysis.

Remember to always adhere to local laws and regulations regarding data protection and privacy when conducting such simulations.<｜end▁of▁sentence｜>

